Required attribution:

  The BeSS consortium (Be Star Spectra database, https://basebe.obspm.fr/),
  using the canonical credit recommended by the archive:

    "This research has made use of the BeSS database, operated at LESIA,
     Observatoire de Paris-Meudon, France: http://basebe.obspm.fr"
     (Neiner et al. 2011)

  together with a citation to this work:
  "BESS-Bench: Benchmarking Spectral Representations for Be-Star Variability", 2026.

  Individual observer names are not redistributed (FITS OBSERVER
  keywords are stripped at export). Aggregate observer information
  (column `observer_type`: amateur / professional / unknown) is
  preserved for statistical analyses; site coordinates are coarsened
  (lat/lon to 0.1 deg, elevation to 100 m) to prevent
  re-identification while supporting hemispheric / air-mass studies.

